# Source and license notice

The KeePass2.61.1 source-assisted recycle-bin/history contracts are copyrighted by Dominik Reichl and the KeePass contributors and licensed under GPL-2.0-or-later. The exact upstream license is preserved at [source-study/selected/Docs/License.txt.snapshot](source-study/selected/Docs/License.txt.snapshot). This work-only source-assisted implementation and its changes are provided under GPL-2.0-or-later. Existing copyright/license notices in copied source and previous accepted modules remain in place.

[source-provenance.json](source-provenance.json) lists16 inert selected source/license snapshots, exact bytes and SHA256s from the authenticated source carrier. The carrier SHA256 is `711bd9ec7076661678469e51bae876debac07a08c32f1b1c6b3b8fe5e761c13a` (5,333,853 bytes;1381 ZIP entries). It was checked against the preserved publisher digest; OpenPGP signature verification is not claimed. The full sourceZIP remains locally preserved in the earlier immutable source-study stage and is not embedded in the candidate.

The actual original portable assembly is used only by synthetic independent test helpers after its release SHA verification. No original executable/DLL code is imported into the application or used to implement its runtime actions. Preserved raw observations contain only synthetic fixture data. All original helper execution, source-composed orchestration, clock adapters and narrower candidate policies are distinguished in the README and run records.
